<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Shared SpotBugs exclusions (template-first: ships verbatim to every
  template-lineage repo; decision + rationale recorded on
  neoforge-mod-template#52).

  EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2: returning or storing a reference to a mutable
  object. In NeoForge mod code that is the idiomatic shape by design - fields
  hold Level, ItemStack, and capability objects because the game model IS
  shared mutable state; upstream SpotBugs has no Minecraft awareness and flags
  the correct pattern as a vulnerability (~45 findings org-wide at flip time,
  all noise).

  Scope rule: these TWO patterns only. Any future addition needs an issue-first
  decision recorded on #52 - this file must never become a dumping ground.
  Everything else (MS_EXPOSE_REP, PA_PUBLIC_PRIMITIVE_ATTRIBUTE, MS_PKGPROTECT,
  and every correctness/security detector) stays enforced everywhere.
-->
<FindBugsFilter>
    <Match>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
